<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria sells 12.97 bln levs 1- and 4-wk T-bills.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria sells 12.97 bln levs 1- and 4-wk T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry on Friday sold two discount T-bill issues with maturities of one week and four weeks, yielding 3.79 percent and 17.72 percent to maturity, respectively, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Bids were received for a total of 12.974 billion levs of T-bills and the ministry approved all of them.</p>
<p>The issues were offered with no par value or minimum acceptable prices set in advance.</p>
<p>Details of the issues follow: @</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3015297008	 BG3015397006</p>
<p> Term			    one week	     four weeks</p>
<p> Auction date		  February 14, 1997  February 14, 1997</p>
<p> Issue date		    February 14, 1997  February 14, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date		 February 21, 1997  March 14, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		 8,064 million levs     4,910 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   96.35 pct	    84.95</p>
<p> Bids approved		 8,064 million levs     4,910 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  96.35 pct	    84.95 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     3.79 pct	     17.72 pct @</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
